 **Escaped-defect rate:** the share of trials whose final repo fails at least
 one hidden-oracle test, or whose oracle fails to build. One value per trial.
+The oracle runs twice on the finished repo, in the dev profile and with
+`--release`; a trial is an escaped defect if it fails in **either**
+(both results are recorded). For two-step tasks (H11, H17) the value is
+taken once, after the last step. A timeout or agent crash is scored by the
+oracle on whatever the repo contains. An oracle test that hits its 10 s
+limit is re-run once, after every other trial of the run has finished and
+with nothing else running; both runs are recorded and the re-run decides
+that test.
+
+**Infrastructure failures are not scored.** A trial whose harness step
+fails (an exception in setup, the agent container or evaluation), whose
+agent session ends on an API, authentication or quota error, that starts
+no session, or whose transcript names a model other than the requested one
+is recorded as an `infra_error` row, excluded from every metric, and run
+again (`run.py --resume`) until it is scored. Infra rows are counted and
+listed in the report.
+
+**Primary comparison:** C − A over all 20 held-out tasks. One primary
