 ## Design
 
 | Item | Setting |
 |---|---|
-| Tasks | Dev split (currently 4): used for tuning the profile and harness. Held-out split (≥ 16, not yet written): oracles written and hashed before the profile is frozen for the run. |
+| Splits | **dev** (T01–T04): harness and profile tuning, never reported as a result. **calibration** (K01–K03): arm A only, used to fix the task style and choose the primary model, never part of any comparison. **held-out** (H01–H20, listed below): the only split this preregistration covers. |
 | Arms | A, B, C, the same tasks for each |
-| Trials | ≥ 5 per task per arm for held-out; 3 for the pilot |
-| Model | One named model and version for the primary analysis. A second model as a replication, reported separately. |
-| Isolation | Fresh container per trial; same turn and time limits for every arm |
-| Order | Trials interleaved across arms to spread provider-side drift |
+| Trials | 10 per task per arm: 20 × 3 × 10 = 600 per model (plus 60 second steps for H11 and H17) |
+| Primary model | **[owner]** exact id, chosen from calibration before the freeze: the model whose calibration arm A escaped-defect rate is nearer 40% |
+| Replication model | **[owner]** exact id (the other candidate); same tasks, arms and limits; reported separately, never pooled |
+| Candidate models | `claude-sonnet-5-5` and Haiku 5.5 (**[owner]** confirm the exact id) |
+| Agent | Claude Code through `bench/agents/claude-code.sh`; CLI version **[owner]** (the `dev.tauten.bench.claude-version` label of the image; 2.1.327 when this draft was written); agent script sha256 in `bench/heldout.lock` |
+| tauten | the `cargo-tauten` built into the image from the frozen commit; profile `crates/tauten-check/rules.toml` and `agents.md` hashed in the lock |
+| Limits | `--max-turns 60`, 900 s wall time per step, spend cap 2 USD per step, the same in every arm; timeouts are recorded |
+| Isolation | Fresh container per agent session that sees only the trial repo, the prompt and the agent script; network only to the model API and crates.io through an allowlisting proxy; evaluation in a separate container with no network (`bench/container/README.md`) |
+| Dependencies | crates.io is reachable for the agent in every arm. Each trial has its own `CARGO_HOME`, used by its agent sessions and mounted into its evaluation container, so a crate the agent added builds offline there |
+| Two-step tasks | The repo is committed after step 1 (in the evaluation container, hooks off), so step 2 starts from a clean tree; diffs are taken against the recorded base commit |
+| Order | Each trial index is one block of every (task, arm) pair, shuffled with seed 20261118; 4 parallel workers |
+| Transcripts | Full stream-json transcript of every session kept with the results; a scan of tool-call paths outside the trial repo is reported |
